Package: bones
Type: Package
Title: Content-Shaped Loading Placeholders for 'shiny' Outputs
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(
    given = "Tanmay",
    family = "Chanda",
    email = "jadevenom2430@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Replaces loading spinners with skeleton placeholders that match
    the shape of the content being loaded, so users can see what is coming
    rather than only that something is happening. Placeholders are inferred
    automatically from the type of 'shiny' output being wrapped, reserve the
    output's layout so that nothing shifts when content arrives, and are shown
    only on first load: when an output is recalculated, the previous content is
    kept on screen and dimmed instead of being replaced.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
    htmltools,
    utils
Suggests:
    shiny (>= 1.7.0),
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
